                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ever since I saw the trailer for this game, I was thrilled for playing it. Some other user, however, made a long and thoughtful review, listing several issues with how the game handled tutorials and how many of its elements didn't seem to clearly point out to the player what they were doing. Years later, namely yesterday, I've decided to give it a chance, 6 years after release. Sadly, all the complaints I saw are still valid. There is no clear tutorial, besides a quick view into military actions. Turns go by where you cannot perform a single action without risking a domestic interest mismanagement, and there seems to be no way out for it besides waiting for the next focus. To make matters worse, I sought the manual, only to find out that, 6 years after launch, it still missing entire sections. This is an egregious botch job, and it pains me to say it. I've already filed for a refund due to this massive disapointment. It should follow naturally that years into DLC development, this should all have been changed. I get that grand strategy games like CK2 and EU struggle with conveying a good tutorial, but the fact that the matter wasn't even addressed was the last straw.",
